{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex","tool":"list_mcp_resources","arguments":{},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"resources\":[{\"server\":\"pexafy\",\"uri\":\"ui://pexafy/grid.html\",\"name\":\"pexafy_results_grid\",\"title\":\"Pexafy results grid\",\"description\":\"The photographs found, as a grid the reader works in: unnumbered thumbnails, a heart on each to like it, a shape filter in the head, and, on a tap, a swipe deck in the grid's own place — one photograph at a time, with its credit, license, kept or skipped with a swipe, and a similar button (the ≈ mark) for more photographs like it. The filter and ≈ re-run the search inside the grid, where the host lets the frame call a tool. The photos they liked stay under the grid, numbered #1..#n.\",\"mimeType\":\"text/html;profile=mcp-app\",\"_meta\":{\"openai/widgetDomain\":\"https://pexafy.com\",\"openai/widgetDescription\":\"The gallery of the photographs found for this request, drawn for the reader with each photograph's credit and licence: the reply needs no picture or link of its own. Thumbnails carry no numbers; a heart on each likes it, a shape filter re-runs the search, and a swipe deck opens in the grid's own place — one photograph at a time, with who took it and what is in it, and a ≈ button that asks for more like it. The photographs the reader liked stay under the grid, numbered #1..#n on screen in the reader's order — the order liked, which they can rearrange by dragging: those are the numbers the reader sees and names them by (“#2”). They are readable through get_grid_selected_photos.\",\"openai/widgetCSP\":{\"resource_domains\":[\"https://thumb.pexafy.com\"],\"connect_domains\":[\"https://mcp.pexafy.com\"]},\"ui\":{\"csp\":{\"connectDomains\":[\"https://mcp.pexafy.com\"],\"resourceDomains\":[\"https://thumb.pexafy.com\"]},\"domain\":\"https://pexafy.com\"},\"fastmcp\":{\"tags\":[]}},\"annotations\":{\"audience\":[\"user\"]}}]}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
